# Ship: branch, PR, merge to main

When the user asks to ship, deploy, redeploy, or put work on `main`:

1. Commit on a **feature branch** (not `main`). Exception to “only commit when asked.”
2. Push the branch to `origin`. Do not `--force` push `main`.
3. Open a **pull request** into `main`.
4. Merge that PR when the user wants it live (they may merge in GitHub, or say to merge).
5. **Stop there.** Coolify Auto Deploy on this resource picks up the push to `main`. Do not tell the user to click **Deploy** unless history stays Manual.

Do **not** push commits straight to `main` unless the user explicitly says to.

Keep `ai-office-backend` in its own repo. Do not commit or push backend files here.

## Coolify Auto Deploy (verified 2026-08-19)

GitHub App **`fjdr-ai-office`** (org install, all repos) posts to Coolify at `https://coolify.fjdresources.com/webhooks/source/github/events`. Repo Settings → Webhooks is empty; that is normal.

Cloudflare Access: dashboard **Coolify Admin Only** stays TOTP. Path **Coolify GitHub webhooks** is Bypass + Everyone on `coolify.fjdresources.com/webhooks/*` (same pattern as n8n). Do not enable the Coolify instance API.

This resource: branch `main`; Advanced → Auto Deploy **Deploy on push (webhooks)**.

Proven: Coolify `ai-office-frontend` history showed **Webhook** Success for merge `7035946` (PR #12) and `254d8f9` (PR #11). Older **Manual** rows are from before the Access bypass.

If a merge does not show as Webhook, check GitHub App **`fjdr-ai-office`** → Advanced → Recent deliveries (expect **200**) and Coolify history. Do **not** fix a miss by enabling the Coolify instance API.

## Production TOTP (backend Coolify)

Login 401 is **not** a frontend bug. Production `docker-compose.yaml` injects **`TOTP_SECRET` only**. Ignore leftover Coolify names `TOTP_SECRET_PROD` / `TOTP_SECRET_TEST` (those are local dual-stack `docker-compose.yml`). Do not enroll from `JWT_SECRET`. Google Authenticator needs Base32 (`A–Z`, `2–7`); strip quotes and `=`. Tracked as [ai-office-backend#15](https://github.com/fjdresources/ai-office-backend/issues/15) and frontend [#6](https://github.com/fjdresources/ai-office-frontend/issues/6).
